# Auth (JWT), read by cmd/server. Every application route requires a bearer token,
# and the server refuses to start if a value below is missing, short or a demo value.
# JWT_SECRET signs and verifies tokens (HS256, at least 32 bytes). gopamin generated
# a random one for this project; in production load it from a secret store.
JWT_SECRET={{.Secrets.JWTSecret}}
JWT_TTL=15m
JWT_ISSUER={{.Name}}
JWT_AUDIENCE={{.Name}}
# Demo login (POST /login), a placeholder for a real user store. The password was
# printed once when the project was generated; only its hash is kept here. Set a
# new one with `make hash-password`.
AUTH_USERNAME=admin
AUTH_PASSWORD_HASH={{.Secrets.AuthPasswordHash}}
